INTERVIEW QUESTION 2
Difference between Generative AI and Traditional AI
===================================================

Interview Answer:

Generative AI creates new content such as text, images, code, audio,
and videos by learning patterns from training data.

Traditional (Discriminative) AI does not generate new content. It
analyzes existing data to perform tasks such as classification,
prediction, recommendation, or detection.

Difference:

## Generative AI

• Creates new content
• Output: Text, code, images, audio, video
• Examples: ChatGPT, GitHub Copilot, DALL·E

## Traditional AI

• Predicts or classifies existing data
• Output: Label, prediction, recommendation
• Examples: Spam detection, Face recognition,
Fraud detection, Disease prediction

Memory Trick:

Generative AI  →  CREATE
Traditional AI →  PREDICT

